+\subsection{Historical Cohort Sensitivity and Prior Evaluation}
+\label{subsec:original276}
+
+The 276-slot retraining tests endpoint sensitivity on a previously exposed historical request list. Seventy-nine requested UIDs overlapped the earlier recorded training list and were removed, leaving 1,039 training UIDs with no requested-list overlap. During evaluation, an empty-input error at requested slot 46 triggered an inherited loader's random replacement whose actual UID was not recorded. The 1,104 rows therefore represent 276 requested slots under four paired conditions, not verified coverage of 276 distinct held-out objects. This panel is reported as a protocol/checkpoint sensitivity analysis; it does not recover the historical main checkpoint or reproduce its reported $+0.96$ dB result.
+
+C3 minus Fixed High is $+1.699$ dB in full-frame PSNR (276/276 slots positive), but $-1.314$ dB in FG-PSNR (9/276 favorable). FG-LPIPS is higher by 0.01127, FG-SSIM lower by 0.05961, and Edge-SSIM lower by 0.02777. Excluding the known failed requested slot preserves the opposing PSNR means ($+1.697$ and $-1.311$ dB) and the LPIPS loss ($+0.01127$). White-background normalization also favors Fixed High. The raw full-frame gain therefore does not support reference-texture fidelity. C3 improves FG-PSNR over Fixed Low by 0.783 dB, while their descriptive FG-LPIPS interval includes zero. Slot-bootstrap diagnostics do not establish independent-object inference because the substituted UID is unknown. Fixed Mean, moved high windows and Generic Linear were not evaluated here, so this panel cannot test temporal allocation.
+The requested-slot condition means (Supplementary Table S36) and paired endpoint contrasts (Supplementary Table S35) remain in Section~S7, with the unknown actual-UID substitution and technical, non-confirmatory scope stated alongside.
+
+The original blinded 3AFC study on thirty objects and twenty-four participants reports C3's overall-quality share as 58.1\% (two-level participant/object-bootstrap interval $[50.1,65.8]\%$). This preference applies to the original stimuli; it does not measure texture fidelity for the retrained checkpoint or unseen baked appearance. Counts and endpoint-specific results are retained in Supplementary Section~S7.
